# gen_fu_l44_pmp_step1b.log -- the CM224 sampler rows and the raw-lock shape
# Produced 2026-09-05T07:16:57Z on soc-l-11 from a detached archive of 24da095
# with this landing's files applied. Sampler corrections to committed covergroups; per LOG-096 a covergroup
# owes render, compile, sample-event and caveat statements, not a trust triad, and no bin moves here.
#
# RENDER: the plan's pass 2 changed coverpoint PROSE only, so the rendered include is unchanged.
#   gen_fcov_codegen --check: up to date
# COMPILE: sources sha256 1105ddfa05dd0163, vcs exit 0
#
# THE FIVE ROWS, each with what it did and what it does now.
# MAJOR-1  cp_outcome compared the RAW attempted cfg byte with the pre byte. The DUT stores neither bits 6:5
#          (pmp_cfg_t has no field for them; rtl/ibex_cs_registers.sv:1429-1437 assigns lock from bit 7, mode
#          from [4:3], RWX from [2:0]) nor W when R is clear under MML=0. So a write differing only in
#          reserved bits left post == pre and was booked ignored_lock on an UNLOCKED entry or under RLB=1,
#          and a W-without-R write carrying reserved bits failed the old "post == (a_b & 8'hfd)" test and was
#          booked written instead of w_dropped. Now a helper computes the byte the DUT WOULD store and the
#          comparison is against that.
# MINOR-1  the executable-lock predicate was L && (X || (!R && W)), which includes RWX=111. The RTL's
#          is_mml_m_exec_cfg (rtl/ibex_cs_registers.sv:164-176) accepts {read,write,exec} in
#          {001, 010, 011, 101} only; I checked all eight encodings and 111 is the ONLY divergence, so a
#          locked all-permissions row IS written under MML. The predicate now names the four.
# MAJOR-2  cp_first_after_reset was ONE run-wide flag cleared by any PMP CSR access, while the plan defines
#          it per CSR. At most one of the four cr_reset_read class bins could read yes per run. It is now a
#          flag per CSR class. The retained log of the original landing claimed no bin of the four groups was
#          unreachable; that sentence is corrected in gen_fu_pmp1_covergroups_corrigendum.log, whose bytes
#          stand beside it rather than editing it.
# MINOR-2  the address cp_outcome read written whenever the readback equalled the attempted value, so a
#          locked RLB=0 entry rewritten with its CURRENT value was booked written though ignored. The outcome
#          is now decided by the PRE-STATE rule and only CONFIRMED by the readback; a disagreement between
#          the two is COUNTED and reported rather than absorbed.
# MINOR-3  NOT FIXED, and stated rather than claimed. The plan wants cp_trap.illegal to mean mcause 2.
#          rvfi_trap is ONE BIT in this TB (gen_rvfi_if.sv:8), so the cause is not on the record, and the
#          model state that carries mcause arrives on a different callback. Any retired trap on a PMP CSR
#          access is booked illegal. That is sound for this DUT, where such an access traps only as an
#          illegal instruction, but it is classification by elimination and not a read of the cause. The
#          review row allowed either a check or a stated caveat; this is the caveat.
# RAW LOCK cp_self_lock and cp_next_cfg now carry the RAW lock bit and cp_rlb carries RLB alone, so the cross
#          of the two expresses the effective lock. Encoding RLB in both made the components dependent and
#          made cr_self_lock.locked_rlb1_written and cr_tor_lock.nl_tor_rlb1_written unreachable. The
#          EFFECTIVE lock remains, used by the outcome rule only, whose plan text still names RLB=0.
#
